WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:13.909
In decibels, gains add up. A signal peaking at minus 12 dBFS that goes through 6 dB of gain comes out peaking at minus 6 dBFS.

2
00:00:14.288 --> 00:00:23.057
Headroom is the distance in decibels between the signal peak and the limit of the stage. With a peak at minus 6 dBFS there are 6 dB of headroom.

3
00:00:23.753 --> 00:00:30.581
If the gain exceeds the headroom, the signal hits the limit and clips: the peaks flatten and distortion appears.

4
00:00:35.632 --> 00:00:43.196
In a chain of stages, gains and attenuations add up in decibels; at every stage you must check that the peak stays below the limit.
